Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Taverley: the tile Corey picked, and a check for the mistake
 I made

I put the portal in the middle of somebody's kitchen. The footprint was level
and no solid loc stood on any of its ten tiles - which is exactly why "no
solid loc" does not mean outdoors: walls sit on tile BOUNDARIES, so the inside
of a house reads as ten free tiles.

Flag bit 4 is the client's remove-roofs flag and it marks every tile under a
roof. That is the only thing in the map that says indoors, and it reads 4 on
all ten of the tiles I chose and 0 on every portal that was placed correctly.
Both portalsite.py and battery group 15 now reject a roofed footprint, and a
mutation moves a portal into a Yanille building to prove it goes red.

Taverley is now m45_54 anchor 7,0 rotated 3 - facing west, which is what was
asked for in the first place and what the last square had nowhere level for.
Spread 5, no roof, no road, landing 6,2 and the agent at 6,1.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK; poh_battery ALL PASS; poh_mutate 94/94 caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
